SUMMARY:MST Walker Knob Overlook/Balsam Gap - Route 128\, 8.5mi\, 2\,300ft
  FITNESS HIKE
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nAccording to the Mt. Mitchell Park
  website\, this trail is now open. If not\, we'll do what we did last time
  and backtrack to the Little Butt overlook. https://www.alltrails.com/trai
 l/us/north-carolina/mount-mitchell-state-park-trail\n\nCar poolers will me
 et in the intersection of the Blue Ridge Parkway and Elk Mountain Scenic H
 ighway\, near Bull Gap at 9:00am. The hike will start at the Walker Knob O
 verlook on the Parkway. Please let the hike leader know where you intend t
 o meet us: carpool spot (9:00am) or trailhead (9:30am).\n\nAny rain cancel
 lation or venue change will be made by 8:00am.\n\nOut and back hike. The t
 rail elevates quickly and then undulates along a ridge of the Black Mounta
 in chain. Expect to see lots of moss\, ferns\, and fungi. Some of the trai
 l is rocky\; some is soft moss and pine needle carpet.\n\nWe will stop for
  lunch at the Allen Rinas overlook\, a rather prominent rock outcropping w
 ith a great view over the Asheville watershed (see photo) near the 4mi poi
 nt\, and turn around there.\n\nMore ambitious hikers are welcome to contin
 ue the approximately one mile (and 350ft.) descent to Route 128\, and turn
  around there.\n\nWe will be near 6\,000ft elevation and under forest cove
 r for most of the hike.\n\nPACE: Fitness hikes proceed at a steady BRISK p
 ace adjusting for steepness of grade. PLEASE BE IN SHAPE AND CAPABLE OF HI
 KING THIS DISTANCE WITH ELEVATION. This is not a hike for beginners. If yo
 ur interests include outdoor fitness hiking for cardio conditioning and en
 durance join us.\n\nDOGS: Dogs are welcome as long as they are trail frien
 dly.\n\nIF YOU SIGN ON THIS HIKE AND CHANGE YOUR MIND (EVEN IF YOU ARE ON 
 THE WAITLIST) GO BACK TO THE RSVP LINK AND CHANGE YOUR STATUS TO FREE UP Y
 OUR RESERVED SPOT.\n\nRelease of Liability:\nThe organizer of this trip is
  volunteer and is not a professional guide. The function of the organizer 
 is only to organize this trip. If you sign up or participate in this event
  you acknowledge that you freely and voluntarily agree to assume all risks
  of injuries\, illnesses and damages arising from\, as a result of and ass
 ociated with this event. In addition\, you acknowledging that you agree to
  the Meetup terms: https://www.meetup.com/terms\n\nThis is a Level 7 hike.
 \n*Hike Levels:Level 1\; 300-600 feet elevation gain\; Level 2 600-900'\; 
 Level 3\, 900-1200"\; Level 4\; 1200-1500' Level 5\; 1500-1800' LEVEL 6\; 
 1800-2100' Level 7*\; 2100-2400' Level 8\; 2400-2700' Level 9\; 2700-3000'
  Level 10\; 3000-4000' ULTIMATE HIKES\; > 4000'
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/314701446
 /
