DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260513T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260513T210000
SUMMARY:Wednesday night Bent Creek
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nHard Times Trailhead near Lake Pow
 hatan Rec Area\nRSVP's don't open until 6PM Sunday night.\nWeather: will k
 now more by Monday and will let everyone know the details then.\nI did thi
 s hike series for many years before 2022\, but I did it as a high-speed hi
 ke\, and I am now doing it as a moderate speed hike. This is a numbers lim
 ited event and I expect people who sign-up to show up. Late cancellations\
 , and those that don't show up are bumping other interested hikers\, and t
 hey will not be allowed on future hikes.\nIf all goes well\, I will try to
  post a hike most weeks\, and for days Tue or Wed\, distance\, and start l
 ocation\, like switching between Hard Times trail-head and Bent Creek Rive
 r Park\, may change.\nThe current route is about 5.5 miles.\nPlease folks\
 , this is intended as a moderate paced hike\, and we'd like all attendees 
 to keep up with the hike leader(s). This hike is intended as a workout hik
 e for people to get in condition to do weekend hikes.\nModerate paced mean
 s 22-24 min miles\, or 2 ½ mph.\nAs such\, we do not take breaks\, take i
 n views\, or snap photos along the way. Please make sure you're able to ke
 ep up with the group. This hike has always served as a good chance to get 
 exercise during the week\, meet new people\, and create interest for weeke
 nd enjoyment hikes. It's a great introduction to the AHG family.\nNo need 
 to RSVP "No" or "not attending" unless changing from a "Yes."\nPlease read
  the full description before RSVPing\, and only sign up if you are sure yo
 u can go. Thanks in advance for keeping your RSVP up-to-date and not being
  a last-minute cancellation or no-show. This is an ongoing issue with Meet
 ups and often keeps people on waitlists from being able to attend our hike
 s.\nHard Times Trailhead near Lake Powhatan Rec Area\nFollow signs off of 
 Brevard Rd (Rt 191) to Lake Powhatan Rec Area. The road is Bent Creek Ranc
 h Rd. to Wesley Branch Rd. Follow signs to Lake Powhatan until you come to
  Hard Times Trailhead on your left\, 2.5 miles. It is very clearly marked.
  Parking is very limited at the trailhead but there’s a paved pull-off j
 ust before the Hard Times trailhead and more parking just beyond at the Le
 dford Branch trailhead. We will access Bent Creek forest by way of Hard Ti
 mes Trail and do some combination of loop and out and back.\nArrive at the
  trailhead BY 6:00. Because it is a weeknight hike\, we are unable to wait
  for latecomers\, fighting daylight.\n\\*\\*\\*If you are running behind\,
  please post a comment on this Meetup page by 5:45 pm. There is no cell se
 rvice at the parking lot\, so if we don't have any advance notice of you r
 unning late by 5:45\, we can't get any notifications at the trailhead and 
 we will not wait for you.\nWe start the hike at 6:00\, rarely do we get mu
 ch later than that.\n• Wear closed-toed footwear appropriate for hiking.
  The trail will consist of dirt\, rocks\, roots\, mud and mulch.\n• Brin
 g plenty of water.\n• Bring rain gear if a chance of rain is in the fore
 cast.\nHeadlamps suggested\n• Dogs on leashes the whole time are welcome
 . This is an active mountain bike area and it can get messy with dogs runn
 ing loose among hikers and mountain bikers.\nPlease make sure to keep your
  RSVP up-to-date. You don't want to be "that person" who cancels last minu
 te or no-shows and keeps someone from joining in if there's a waitlist. Th
 anks for your consideration - it is appreciated!\nFeel free to post questi
 ons not covered in this description in the comments section.\nThanks - we'
 ll see you on the trail!\nDisclaimer and Release of Liability:\nThis activ
 ity involves hiking on city streets that may have traffic and/or natural t
 rails with roots\, rocks\, and steep sections. Participants are responsibl
 e for their safety on streets and trails. The organizer of this trip is a 
 volunteer and not a professional guide. The function of the organizer is o
 nly to organize this trip. If you sign up or participate in this event you
  acknowledge that you freely and voluntarily agree to assume all risks of 
 injuries\, illnesses\, and damages arising from\, as a result of\, and ass
 ociated with this event. In addition\, you acknowledge that you agree to t
 he Meetup terms: [https://www.meetup.com/terms](https://www.meetup.com/ter
 ms)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/314661389
 /
